  "title": "Banking",
  "text": "thumbThe concept of Banking is to store items in a storage bank to retrieve at another time. Banking solves many issues such as builders storing unneeded furniture in bulk. This feature was introduced on December 4th, 2012.\nStorage\nEach player starts with 25 slots of storage, this can store up to 25 individual items. Same items that are the same tint can also be stacked in one slot. Players can purchase additional slots through the Station Cash Marketplace or the Coin Shop.For the Coin Shop upgrades, it is required that the upgrades be purchased in chronological order.\n2-Slot Bank Upgrade 1 - \n4-Slot Bank Upgrade 2 - \n6-Slot Bank Upgrade 3 - \n8-Slot Bank Upgrade 4 - \n10-Slot Bank Upgrade 5 - \n20-Slot Bank Upgrade 6 - \n40-Slot Bank Upgrade 7 - \n60-Slot Bank Upgrade 8 - \n80-Slot Bank Upgrade 9 - \n100-Slot Bank Upgrade 10 - \nWhereas the SC Marketplace upgrade contains no limit on amount purchased\n50-Slot Bank Upgrade - \nAdditionally players with a Membership that logged on during the month of June 2013 also received 200 free storage slots being apart of the June 2013's Monthly Membership Pack.\nStoring\nTo store items, it is required to either visit a Robgoblin Banker or a Storage Vault. The Robgoblin Bankers are marked on the atlas and can be teleported to.\nBurglz in Seaside near the Seaside Post Office.\nBezzle in Sanctuary near Poe Tatters.\nYoink in Snowhill near the Snowhill Post Office.\nAdditionally players with a Membership that logged on during the month of June 2013 also received a free Storage Vault being apart of the June 2013's Monthly Membership Pack.The Storage Vault is a Housing item and can be placed in a Lot. From there, players can access their storage slots from clicking on the Storage Vault.\nCategory:Guides"
 },
